# Relay writes files with \n and compares diffs byte-for-byte, so a checkout
# that rewrote line endings would make its own tests fail — and, worse, make a
# run's diff disagree with git. Windows clones default to core.autocrlf=true,
# which is exactly that rewrite; this pins every text file to LF in the working
# tree on every platform, so no contributor has to know to turn it off.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and binary-ish artifacts git should not try to reason about.
*.patch -text
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
